{
  "id": "triangle",
  "questionId": "triangle",
  "slug": "triangle",
  "title": "Triangle Minimum Path Sum",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Dp 2d",
  "patterns": [
    "dynamic programming",
    "grid"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "interview-150"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "it's easier to think about this bottom-up: what's the cheapest way to finish a path starting from some cell in the bottom row? just its own value, since there's nowhere left to go",
    "define dp[i][j] as the minimum sum of a path from cell (i, j) down to the bottom of the triangle",
    "recurrence: dp[i][j] = triangle[i][j] + min(dp[i+1][j], dp[i+1][j+1]), since from (i, j) you can only move to (i+1, j) or (i+1, j+1)",
    "start dp equal to the bottom row itself, then work upward row by row applying the recurrence",
    "the answer ends up at dp[0][0], the minimum cost of a path starting at the very top"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "trying to index the next row incorrectly, off by one, since each row has one more element than the row above it",
    "working top-down without memoization, causing the same subpaths to be recomputed exponentially many times",
    "confusing which two children a cell can move to (it's j and j+1 in the row below, not j-1 and j)"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a triangular arrangement of numbers `triangle`, stored as a list of rows where row i has i + 1 elements. Starting at the top and moving down one row at a time, you may move from index j in the current row to either index j or index j + 1 in the next row.\n\n**Find the minimum possible sum of numbers along any path from the top to the bottom row.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= triangle.length <= 200",
      "triangle[i].length == i + 1",
      "-10^4 <= triangle[i][j] <= 10^4"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "a triangle with a single row (just the top element)",
      "all negative numbers",
      "a two-row triangle where every choice matters equally little"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "triangle = [[2],[3,4],[6,5,7],[4,1,8,3]]",
        "output": "11",
        "expectedOutput": "11",
        "explanation": "The path 2 -> 3 -> 5 -> 1 sums to 11 and is the cheapest route."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "triangle = [[-10]]",
        "output": "-10",
        "expectedOutput": "-10",
        "explanation": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "triangle = [[1],[2,3]]",
        "output": "3",
        "expectedOutput": "3",
        "explanation": "The only paths are 1 -> 2 (sum 3) and 1 -> 3 (sum 4); 3 is the minimum."
      }
    ],
